## 4. Data Model — [PuzzleBlock](file:///c:/Users/chitt/Documents/ParsonPuzzle/backend/app/models/puzzle_block.py#13-36)

```python
class PuzzleBlock(BaseModel):
    block_id: str = Field(default_factory=lambda: str(uuid4()))
    puzzle_id: str
    text: str                         # Code line/segment shown to student
    correct_position: int             # Ground-truth order (0-indexed)
    block_type: BlockType = BlockType.NORMAL   # NORMAL | DECOY
    explanation: Optional[str] = None
    indentation_level: int = 0        # Leading spaces count
    is_comment: bool = False
    line_number: int = 0              # Original source line
    created_at: datetime
```

---

## 5. Evaluation Engine — [EvaluationEngine](file:///c:/Users/chitt/Documents/ParsonPuzzle/backend/app/services/evaluation_engine.py#5-178)

The engine validates the submission format, computes an exact-match score (all blocks in correct order = 1.0) and a partial score (fraction of blocks in correct positions), then generates per-block mismatch feedback.

```python
@staticmethod
def evaluate_attempt(submitted_order, puzzle_blocks):
    is_valid, error = EvaluationEngine.validate_submission_format(submitted_order, puzzle_blocks)
    if not is_valid:
        return {"is_correct": False, "score": 0.0, "feedback": {"error": error}}
    is_correct    = EvaluationEngine.compute_exact_match_score(submitted_order, puzzle_blocks)
    partial_score = EvaluationEngine.compute_partial_score(submitted_order, puzzle_blocks)
    feedback      = EvaluationEngine.generate_feedback(submitted_order, puzzle_blocks, is_correct)
    return {"is_correct": is_correct, "score": 1.0 if is_correct else partial_score, "feedback": feedback}
```

