## 7. Frontend — Puzzle Solve Page ([PuzzleSolvePage.jsx](file:///c:/Users/chitt/Documents/ParsonPuzzle/frontend/src/components/student/PuzzleSolvePage.jsx))

Uses **@dnd-kit** for drag-and-drop between two panels: **Block Bank** (right) and **Code Editor** (left).

The page manages two block lists — `editorBlocks` (the student's arranged solution) and `bankBlocks` (the pool of unused blocks). A live timer tracks elapsed time. On submit, only the ordered list of `block_id`s is sent to the backend.

#### Cross-container Drag (Bank ↔ Editor)
```jsx
const handleDragOver = ({ active, over }) => {
    const fromContainer = findContainer(active.id);
    const toContainer   = findContainer(over.id);
    if (!fromContainer || !toContainer || fromContainer === toContainer) return;
    setEditorBlocks(editor => {
        const newEditor = [...editor];
        setBankBlocks(bank => {
            const newBank  = [...bank];
            const fromList = fromContainer === 'editor' ? newEditor : newBank;
            const toList   = toContainer   === 'editor' ? newEditor : newBank;
            const [moved]  = fromList.splice(fromList.findIndex(b => b.block_id === active.id), 1);
            const overIdx  = toList.findIndex(b => b.block_id === over.id);
            toList.splice(overIdx >= 0 ? overIdx : toList.length, 0, moved);
            return [...newBank];
        });
        return [...newEditor];
    });
};
```

